    },
    "configuration": {
      "title": "APICircle Studio",
      "properties": {
        "apicircle.execution.host": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "remote",
            "local"
          ],
          "default": "remote",
          "description": "Whether localhost executes against the extension host (typical) or tunnels to the user's machine via VS Code port forwarding (Remote-SSH / Codespaces only)."
        },
        "apicircle.execution.timeoutMs": {
          "type": "number",
          "default": 30000,
          "description": "Hard timeout in milliseconds for a single request send."
        },
        "apicircle.history.retentionDays": {
          "type": "number",
          "default": 30,
          "description": "Days to retain request and plan run history."
        },
        "apicircle.history.maxEntriesPerWorkspace": {
          "type": "number",
          "default": 500,
          "description": "Max history entries kept per workspace before oldest are evicted."
        },
        "apicircle.mock.defaultPort": {
          "type": [
            "number",
            "null"
          ],
          "default": null,
          "description": "Default port when starting a mock server (null = pick a free port)."
        },
        "apicircle.mcp.autoConfigureClients": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "claude-desktop",
              "claude-code",
              "cursor",
              "windsurf",
              "zed",
              "continue"
            ]
          },
          "default": [],
          "uniqueItems": true,
          "markdownDescription": "**(Phase 8 + 11)** List of AI clients to target when the **Install MCP for All Configured Clients** command runs. Each entry tells APICircle to merge an `apicircle` MCP server entry into that client's user-level config file (e.g. `~/.cursor/mcp.json`, `~/.continue/config.yaml`). Empty by default — the bulk command prompts you with a multi-pick if no clients are configured. Supported: `claude-desktop`, `claude-code`, `cursor`, `windsurf`, `zed`, and (Phase 11) `continue` (YAML config). Cline is not auto-configurable — it reads workspace `.vscode/mcp.json` so use **Install for Copilot Chat / VS Code MCP** instead."
        },
        "apicircle.mcp.allowDecrypt": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": false,
          "markdownDescription": "**(Phase 6+ — deferred)** When true, MCP tools may receive decrypted secret values from the active workspace's vault. Off by default for safety — today MCP clients only see encrypted `enc:v1:` wires. Requires the vault to be unlocked. Wiring this means the security model has to gate per-tool access — that work lands in Phase 6 alongside the in-extension MCP host."
        },
        "apicircle.editor.defaultView": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "text",
            "visual",
            "split"
          ],
          "default": "text",
          "enumDescriptions": [
            "Open APICircle files as YAML text (recommended).",
            "Open APICircle files in the visual editor by default.",
            "Open YAML and visual editors side-by-side automatically."
          ],
          "markdownDescription": "**(Phase 6+ — deferred)** Default editor view for APICircle YAML files. The visual editor lands as part of the Phase 6 opt-in webview workstream; until then the extension is all-native YAML."
        },
        "apicircle.secrets.autoLockMinutes": {
          "type": "number",
          "default": 30,
          "minimum": 0,
          "markdownDescription": "Auto-lock the secret vault after this many minutes of inactivity. `0` = never auto-lock. Changes take effect immediately for already-unlocked vaults."
        },
        "apicircle.secrets.clipboardClearSeconds": {
          "type": "number",
          "default": 30,
          "minimum": 0,
          "markdownDescription": "Clear a revealed secret from the clipboard after this many seconds. `0` = never clear. The clipboard is only cleared if it still holds the value that was copied (you can paste freely without the timer wiping the buffer)."
        },
        "apicircle.secrets.rememberOnDevice": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": false,
          "markdownDescription": "**(Phase 8)** Remember the vault passphrase on this device via VS Code's SecretStorage (backed by OS keychain — Keychain on macOS, Credential Manager on Windows, libsecret on Linux). When enabled, after a successful unlock the passphrase is persisted; the next time you open the workspace the vault unlocks silently. **Security tradeoff:** anyone with access to your OS keychain can read the passphrase, so this should only be enabled on a trusted, encrypted-at-rest device. Disabled by default. Use the **APICircle: Forget Vault Credentials on This Device** command to wipe the stored entry."
        },
        "apicircle.mcp.embeddedHost.enabled": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": false,
          "markdownDescription": "**(Phase 10)** Run an in-extension MCP server over Streamable HTTP. When enabled, the extension exposes the 78-tool MCP catalog on a local loopback port that AI clients (Copilot Chat, Cursor, Claude Desktop with the HTTP transport) can connect to directly — no separate `apicircle-mcp` binary required. Off by default. **Security:** binds ONLY to loopback (`127.0.0.1` / `::1`); bearer-token auth on every request; DNS-rebinding protection via Host-header validation; token rotates on every **Restart**. Use **APICircle: Copy Embedded MCP Host URL** to share the connection URL (incl. token) with your AI client."
        },
        "apicircle.mcp.embeddedHost.port": {
          "type": "number",
          "default": 0,
          "minimum": 0,
          "maximum": 65535,
          "markdownDescription": "**(Phase 10)** Port the embedded MCP host binds to. `0` = let the OS pick a free port (recommended, the chosen port is shown in the MCP view). Set explicitly if you've pre-configured your AI client with a fixed port."
        },
        "apicircle.mcp.embeddedHost.bindHost": {
          "type": "string",
          "default": "127.0.0.1",
          "markdownDescription": "**(Phase 10)** Host interface the embedded MCP host binds to. **Must be a loopback address** (`127.0.0.1`, `localhost`, `::1`, or any `127.x.y.z`). Any non-loopback value is rejected at startup — binding to a non-loopback interface would expose the workspace's MCP tools to the network and is never safe."
        },
        "apicircle.mcp.binaryPath": {
          "type": "string",
          "default": "apicircle-mcp",
          "markdownDescription": "Path to the `apicircle-mcp` binary that external AI clients launch as their MCP server. Defaults to `apicircle-mcp` (assumes the binary is on `PATH`, installed via `pnpm install -g @apicircle/mcp-server`). Set to an absolute path if you installed the binary in a non-standard location."
        },
        "apicircle.mcp.workspaceConfigPath": {
          "type": "string",
          "default": ".vscode/mcp.json",
          "markdownDescription": "Path (relative to the workspace folder) where the **Install for Copilot Chat / VS Code MCP** command writes the workspace-level MCP config. Default `.vscode/mcp.json` is the standard location VS Code 1.86+ Copilot Chat reads automatically. Override only if your project uses a non-standard location."
        },
        "apicircle.validation.validateOnSend": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": true,
          "description": "Run pre-send validation before every send."
        },
        "apicircle.enableMarketplace": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": false,
          "description": "Enable the Marketplace view (placeholder until content is available)."
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "scripts": {
    "build": "tsup",
    "check": "tsc --noEmit",
